.TH XUR.STD.REFLECT 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.reflect \- runtime reflection and binary layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::reflect;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::reflect
inspects and manipulates values at runtime: listing fields, reading and
writing them by name, calling methods dynamically, and reading/writing
structs as binary data through layouts.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B type_name(value) -> str
The type name of a value (e.g.\& "Point", "Shape::Circle", "list").
.TP
.B fields(value) -> [str]
The names of the value's fields (numbers for tuples).
.TP
.B has_field(value, name) -> bool
Whether the value has a field with this name.
.TP
.B get(value, name) -> Value
Read a field by name.
.TP
.B try_get(value, name) -> Option<Value>
Read a field by name, returning
.B None
if it doesn't exist.
.TP
.B set(value, name, new_value) -> Value
Return a copy of the value with one field changed.
.TP
.B variant(value) -> Option<str>
The variant name of an enum value (e.g.\& "Circle" for Shape::Circle).
.TP
.B methods(value) -> [str]
List the value's methods.
.TP
.B has_method(value, name) -> bool
Whether the value has a method with this name.
.TP
.B call(value, name, args) -> Value
Call a method by name with a list of arguments.
.SS Layout
Layouts describe where a struct's fields sit in memory, for reading and
writing binary data. They come from struct attributes or are built at
runtime.
.TP
.B layout::<T>() -> Layout
Get the layout of a Xur struct from its type and attributes.
.TP
.B layout_of(value) -> Layout
Get the layout of a struct value.
.TP
.B Layout::new(name) -> Layout
Start building a layout at runtime.
.PP
Layout methods (each returns a new layout):
.TP
.B layout.field(name, type) -> Layout
Add a field of a primitive type ("u8", "u32", "f64", "bool", etc).
.TP
.B layout.field_at(name, type, offset) -> Layout
Add a field at an explicit byte offset.
.TP
.B layout.bytes(name, len) -> Layout
Add a fixed-length raw byte field.
.TP
.B layout.nested(name, inner_layout) -> Layout
Add a nested struct field.
.TP
.B layout.packed() -> Layout
No padding between fields.
.TP
.B layout.big_endian() -> Layout
.TQ
.B layout.little_endian() -> Layout
Set the byte order for integer and float fields.
.TP
.B layout.aligned(n) -> Layout
Set minimum alignment.
.PP
Layout properties:
.BR name() ,
.BR size() ,
.BR align() ,
.BR is_big_endian() ,
.BR fields() ,
.BR offset_of(name) .
.PP
Reading and writing:
.TP
.B layout.read(data, offset) -> Value
Read a struct from bytes at the given offset.
.TP
.B layout.from_bytes(data) -> Value
Read a struct from the start of bytes.
.TP
.B layout.write(data, offset, value)
Write a struct's fields into a byte buffer.
.TP
.B layout.to_bytes(value) -> bytes
Serialize a value to bytes.
.SS Struct attributes for layout
.nf
#[repr(C)]             // C layout (default)
#[repr(packed)]        // no padding
#[repr(align(8))]      // minimum alignment
#[endian(Big)]         // byte order (Little by default)
#[field(offset = 8)]   // explicit field offset
#[field(size = 16)]    // fixed byte count (for bytes fields)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::reflect;
use std::io;

struct Point { x: i64, y: i64 }

fn main() {
    let p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };
    io::println("fields: {}", reflect::fields(p));
    io::println("x = {}", reflect::get(p, "x"));

    let layout = reflect::layout::<Point>();
    io::println("{}", layout);
    let data = layout.to_bytes(p);
    let p2 = layout.from_bytes(data);
    io::println("round-trip: {}", p2);
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.any (7),
.BR xur.std.mem (7)
